Keep completed movie source playback successful after reset warnings.

Wine ALSA reset warns on drop/reset/prepare errors, still tries each call,
clears the client's queue and returns S_OK. Actual Wine MCI with unchanged
short original AVI packets completes and closes after both ALSA reset calls
are deliberately failed with EIO. Native's empty-queue reset short-circuited
on that error and reported a movie failure despite fully consumed source PCM.

Try the entire completed-queue reset and latch source completion regardless
of its transport warnings. Later driver-silence failures must not change that
completed-source result. Caller-data write errors remain errors. This fixes
the observed completion policy, not whole device tails or shared A/V clocks.

--- a/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
+++ b/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
@@ -80,9 +80,11 @@
             /* WINMM stops/resets an empty completed header queue independently
              * of MCI's later drain poll/close. Discard its initial lead-in. */
             if(!movie_alsa.source_done){
-                if(movie_snd_pcm_drop(movie_alsa.device)<0 ||
-                   movie_snd_pcm_reset(movie_alsa.device)<0 ||
-                   movie_snd_pcm_prepare(movie_alsa.device)<0)return -1;
+                /* Wine ALSA logs these errors, tries every step, and returns
+                 * S_OK. The caller source has already completed playback. */
+                movie_snd_pcm_drop(movie_alsa.device);
+                movie_snd_pcm_reset(movie_alsa.device);
+                movie_snd_pcm_prepare(movie_alsa.device);
                 movie_alsa.source_done=1;
             }
             return 0; /* one driver silence period per producer tick */
@@ -99,7 +101,7 @@
         if(SDL_AtomicGet(&movie_alsa.stop))break;
         SDL_LockMutex(movie_alsa.mutex);
         if(SDL_AtomicGet(&movie_alsa.stop)){SDL_UnlockMutex(movie_alsa.mutex);break;}
-        if(movie_alsa_fill())movie_alsa.error=1;
+        if(movie_alsa_fill() && !movie_alsa.source_done)movie_alsa.error=1;
         SDL_UnlockMutex(movie_alsa.mutex);
         if(movie_alsa.error)break;
     }
